  "articleBody": "When you're planning accessible bathroom modifications, it's really all about making your space work better for *you*. First off, think about the specific bathroom tasks that are giving you trouble right now. Are you struggling to get into the shower? Is the toilet too low? These details will help guide your choices. Next, decide whether a curbless shower or a walk-in tub is a better fit for your needs and preferences. Also, don't forget to consider where you'll need transfer and cleanup space, especially if you're using a wheelchair or other mobility aids. A small but important detail is whether controls should be left- or right-oriented for the primary user – it makes a huge difference in daily convenience. Prioritizing secure mounting for things like grab bars, ensuring slip resistance with your flooring, and having sufficient clearances for movement are all key. And definitely look for hardware that's easy to use, even with limited grip strength. If your modifications involve structural support, plumbing, or electrical work, getting professional input from a company like HH Remodeling LLC can really help avoid any unsafe or unusable changes.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}